  "comments": "Introduced in 2008 when the small coinage designs were changed from the Emblems of Britain to the Royal Shield of Arms.<br /><br />\r\nInformation received from the Royal Mint circulating coin team:<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">‘The issue date for nickel-plated steel 5 and 10 pence pieces was originally intended to be January 2011, however this was deferred to January 2012 to allow additional time for automatic vending machines to be updated to accept the coins. As a result, the 2011 dated 5 and 10 pence pieces were issued into circulation in 2012 instead.’</span><br /><br />\r\nVariants found by Steve Leach<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/560d375e7176f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/560d375e7176f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"149\" /></a><br />\r\nOle<br />\r\nI have found similar variants in the 2015 version",
